<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Put the company facility onto RimWorld's OWN map for the tile the player picked.

       Owner direction, 2026-09-30: **"the map generator is not our mod"** — after reporting
       *"its not the tilemap i chose the land features are all barren to just bare dirt not even
       vegitation"* on a tile chosen with **Map Preview** (`m00nl1ght.MapPreview`).

       Until 0.12.46-dev this mod set `Find.GameInitData.mapGeneratorDef` to a generator of its
       own with four steps. Core's `Base_Player` inherits `MapCommonBase` and runs the whole
       chain: elevation, fertility, biome terrain, caves, rocks from grid, plants, animals,
       ruins, rivers, roads, plus the Royalty, Biotech and Anomaly steps. Replacing it produced
       flat Soil with a building on it, and **Map Preview simulates the real generator**, so the
       preview a player rerolled against was a picture of a map the mod discarded. The preview
       was right; the game was wrong.

       WHY THIS IS AN ADD RATHER THAN A REPLACE. `PatchOperationAdd` appends to the existing
       list, so every one of Core's steps and every step any other mod has added to
       `Base_Player` still runs. A `PatchOperationReplace` here would take ownership of the list
       and silently drop other mods' steps — and `check-compliance.py` refuses destructive
       operations outright for exactly that reason.

       WHY THIS IS SAFE ON EVERY OTHER MAP. `Base_Player` runs for **every** player map a game
       ever generates: a second settlement, a quest site, a reloaded world. Both steps below
       call `HeadquartersBuilder.StartForMap`, which returns **null** — not a throw — unless the
       map is the initial company start on the tile the player chose and no branch exists yet.
       They return immediately in every other case. That guard used to throw, which was fine
       while nothing but our own generator could reach it and is the thing that had to change
       before this patch could exist.

       The gen step ORDER values decide when they run, not this list: terrain at 5, before
       Core's own terrain work, and the facility at 800, after rocks and before ruins. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RR_HeadquartersTerrain</li>
      <li>RR_HeadquartersFacility</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
